# nr-office-pdf-render-pages: renderPdfPages in mixdog-office-pdf (src/render.rs, src/contact_sheets.rs)

Not compiled: cargo was not run (the lead compiles the wave). The two modules are not part of the crate until the lines below are applied.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-pdf/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod analysis;` (keep the list sorted: `analysis`, `contact_sheets`, `document`, `limits`, `render`, `search`):

    pub mod contact_sheets;

and after `pub mod limits;`:

    pub mod render;

After the last `pub use` line add:

    pub use render::{
        ContactSheet, PageImage, RenderPagesOptions, RenderedImage, RenderedPages, SheetPage, VisualCoverage,
        render_pdf_pages,
    };

(The doc comment at the top of lib.rs may name `pdf-render.mjs` among the ported files.)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office-pdf/Cargo.toml

[dependencies], keeping the list sorted, add (all are workspace dependencies; none is a new crate, only new edges of
mixdog-office-pdf: mixdog-fonts, mixdog-office-base (WriteNote), mixdog-rt, tracing):

    mixdog-fonts = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-rt = { workspace = true }
    tracing = { workspace = true }

[dev-dependencies], add (the twin test runs lane jobs on the inline test backend and drives the async call):

    mixdog-rt = { workspace = true, features = ["test-support"] }
    tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt"] }

`cargo update --workspace --offline` and `cargo hakari generate` only add these edges to the lock and to mixdog-workspace-hack's
feature unification if hakari wants it. No external crate beyond the lock is used (base64, serde_json are already dependencies).

