## What callers must know

- Entry point: `render_pdf_pages(lanes: LaneTokens, registry: Arc<Registry>, note: Arc<dyn WriteNote>, path: &Path,
  options: RenderPagesOptions) -> Result<RenderedPages, AnalysisError>` (async; the caller passes the process's lane tokens, the font
  registry its canvases use, and the call's write ledger as the `WriteNote`). `RenderedPages::to_json()` is Node's result object.
  The adapter task that replaces `renderPdfPages` callers (read-special-files, docx-html-runner, benchmark, office-actions-batch,
  preview-stage, pdf-ocr) maps `maximumScale: 3` (chart pictures) to `RenderPagesOptions.maximum_scale` and `writeImages: false`
  to `write_images`.
- Text on the page itself: `render_page` is called with `fonts: None, drawing: None` because nothing in the tree implements
  `mixdog_pdf::oplist::FontProvider` or `mixdog_pdf::render::FontDrawing` (see nr-office-pdf-render-core.wire, "What the rasteriser
  needs from other tasks"). Until that font bridge exists the glyphs of a page are not drawn (the painter says so once); the page
  numbers of the bottom band are repainted by this task from the text layer and do appear. When the bridge exists, `paint_page` in
  render.rs passes its `FontProvider` and `FontDrawing` in the two `RenderOptions` fields.
- A canvas with no registered font (an empty `Registry`) draws no page numbers and no sheet labels: the reason is reported once at
  error level and the render goes on; the registry the caller passes should be the process's scanned system fonts.

No service, protocol method or SERVICE_PENDING name comes from this task.
